              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for to split, then the Telugu for to break off."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: అరిగిపోవు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అరిగిపోవు — arigipōvu — \"to wear down; to wear out\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఎక్కువ నడవడంతో నా చెప్పులు అరిగిపోయాయి. ekkuva naḍavaḍantō nā ceppulu arigipōyāyi. With so much walking, my sandals have worn down."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): అరిగిపోయింది, arigipōyindi."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Said of soles, tyres and steps worn thin by use. Its subject is a thing, so the past shown is the third person: అరిగిపోయింది, it wore down."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అరిగిపోవు (arigipōvu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 316 lists Telugu aṟugu, \"to wear away, to waste away; to be digested\", here with పోవు, \"to go\" (DEDR 4572), which marks a change that is complete."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
